#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064152 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064035 :question/id #uuid "b7051104-6e23-5ab2-8779-5d54a3c3f5f5" :question/math-academy-id "e-270" :question/problem "Consider a spherical balloon with radius $r.$ As the balloon loses air, its volume $V$ decreases. What is the best interpretation of $V'(r)?$\n\n![](images/7f/7f52288ca4670375413ecd5283bc2d15fbb332af311ead07986c1526d25e338a.png)" :question/worked-solution "The function $V(r)$ gives the volume of a sphere with radius $r.$ So\n\n$$\nV'(r) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}V}{\\textrm{d}r} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{Change in }V}{\\textrm{Change in }r}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $V'(r)$ is the rate at which the volume changes as the radius changes."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "159b4d58-b34d-52cd-aad2-2c058f772ad2" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049362 :topic/math-academy-id 337 :topic/title "The Instantaneous Rate of Change of a Function at a Point"}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517305 :question-generator/id #uuid "2e7d7756-d35c-521b-911d-12b0d2b502d2" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186064152.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ec57e68-f96f-5b48-b52c-8b36af1420aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The area of a circle with radius $r$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063044} {:answer/id #uuid "ed2f68c6-cc44-5265-950e-997a1aa2ad3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the radius changes as the area changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063045} {:answer/id #uuid "f2762674-a011-5f07-98aa-edaec50b70d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The length of the radius of the circle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063046} {:answer/id #uuid "0dc27870-8a25-53e7-873e-b2b72c41ee2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circumference of the 