answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the major axis changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244351} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d129f8a-681e-53f4-b910-966663b5b595" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246792}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "45b2e799-d000-5801-973f-7fb80701d236" :question/math-academy-id "q-112063" :question/problem "Consider an ellipse such that its major axis $a$ can vary while its minor axis is fixed. What is the best interpretation of ${S}^{′}(a)$ if $S$ is the area enclosed by the ellipse?" :question/worked-solution "The function $S(a)$ gives the area of the ellipse with major axis $a.$ So,\n\n$$\n{S}^{′}(a)=\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}a}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }S}{\\text{Change in }a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${S}^{′}(a)$ is the rate at which the area changes as the major axis changes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a3c608b-0776-5682-807c-c217199505fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The length of each side of the cube" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327849} {:answer/id #uuid "821f7ab3-b9fa-5e2e-874b-4fb96cb126a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which each side changes as the volume changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328056} {:answer/id #uuid "a04c5fbf-fabc-5b22-b73b-1f7f7eb0701c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the volume changes as each side changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328321} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c51007-5a0a-5a87-9323-57b4562c0a35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The volume of a cube with side $s$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328826} {:answer/id #uuid "f87b7a58-612c-5146-a7cc-b44d08303d5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the surface area of the cube changes as each side changes" :db/i